# Benchmark report: rabbithole-relevance

2026-08-15 21:04 UTC · qwen3.5:4b via ollama · think on · batch 8 · 2 runs
5 of 12 samples (--limit 5) · 1m1.8s · 6.18s/sample
profile 4f2a9c1b8e3d · prompt 9a1c33bd0e12 · benchmark 71b2c9ff41aa

This is for tuning, not grading. No model will match the golden marks perfectly. What matters is whether an edit moves the dial. If results are far off, your profile or system prompt may be worth fine-tuning.

> **The model returned no score for 1 of 5 samples. They are counted here and excluded from every metric, rather than read as a zero.**

## Scoring

4 scored, 1 unanswered · QWK volatile below 30 samples

| metric | value | range | measures |
|---|---|---|---|
| QWK | +0.47 | -1..1 up | agreement beyond what chance alone gives |
| MAE | 1.75 | 0..10 down | mean distance from the golden score |
| RMSE | 2.60 | 0..10 down | the same, weighting big misses more |
| SIGNED MEAN | -1.25 | -10..10 ->0 | which way the model leans overall |

## Is the high-signal tier trustworthy?

At the 7+ mark the feed page badges as high signal. Nothing is hidden below it, so this is about whether the badge tells the truth rather than what reaches the page.

| metric | value | range | measures |
|---|---|---|---|
| PRECISION | — | 0..1 up | of what it badges, how much you want |
| RECALL | 0.00 | 0..1 up | of what you want, how much it badges |

- the model badges **0**; golden says **2** deserve it
- nothing reached the mark, so the tier would have been empty
- recall **0.00** — it misses 2 of the 2 that do

At other marks:

| mark | badged | wanted | precision | chance | recall |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 3+ | 3 | 3 | 1.00 | 0.75 | 1.00 |
| 4+ | 3 | 3 | 1.00 | 0.75 | 1.00 |
| 5+ | 1 | 2 | 1.00 | 0.50 | 0.50 |
| 6+ | 1 | 2 | 1.00 | 0.50 | 0.50 |
| 7+ | 0 | 2 | — | 0.50 | 0.00 |
| 8+ | 0 | 1 | — | 0.25 | 0.00 |
| 9+ | 0 | 1 | — | 0.25 | 0.00 |

CHANCE is the precision a scorer picking at random would reach at that mark.

